<title>POLAND: BOS falls 4.2 pct on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>BOS falls 4.2 pct on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish Bank Ochrony Srodowiska (BOS) fell 4.2 percent to 46 zlotys in profit-taking after it debuted on Monday 65.5 percent higher than its issue price, traders said.</p>
<p>Turnover amounted to 3.9 zlotys.</p>
<p>&quot;Those who bought the stock at 29 zlotys issue price are taking profits,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Some analysts said the stock was likely to extend its loss on Wednesday, but said it could rebound later, expecting the stock to swing in the channel of between 42 and 52 zlotys.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
